# {{project_name}}

A wrapped-asset contract that mints a wrapper balance on deposit and burns it
on withdraw, 1:1 with an underlying SEP-41 token, generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`wrapped-asset` template.

## How it works

1. **Wrap** — deposit `amount` of the underlying token; the contract locks
   it and credits your wrapper balance by `amount`.
2. **Unwrap** — burn `amount` of wrapper balance; the contract releases
   `amount` of the underlying token back to you.
3. **Conservation** — the total wrapper supply always equals the underlying
   token balance held by the contract.

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then initialize with the underlying token:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <ADMIN> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --underlying <UNDERLYING_TOKEN_ADDRESS>
```

Wrap and unwrap:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <USER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- wrap \
  --from <USER_ADDRESS> \
  --amount 1000000

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <USER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- unwrap \
  --from <USER_ADDRESS> \
  --amount 1000000
```

